", "bbox": [201.13499450683594, 168.51797485351562, 215.0183868408203, 203.10812377929688]}, {"text": "1.4", "bbox": [237.58399963378906, 168.51797485351562, 251.4674072265625, 203.10812377929688]}, {"text": "1.5", "bbox": [274.03399658203125, 168.51797485351562, 287.9173889160156, 203.10812377929688]}, {"text": "1.6", "bbox": [310.4840087890625, 168.51797485351562, 324.36737060546875, 203.10812377929688]}, {"text": "1.7", "bbox": [346.9330139160156, 168.51797485351562, 360.8163757324219, 203.10812377929688]}, {"text": "1.8", "bbox": [383.38299560546875, 168.51797485351562, 397.2663879394531, 203.10812377929688]}, {"text": "1.9", "bbox": [419.8320007324219, 168.51797485351562, 433.71636962890625, 203.10812377929688]}, {"text": "1.10", "bbox": [453.4339904785156, 168.51797485351562, 473.0159912109375, 203.10812377929688]}, {"text": "Total", "bbox": [498.989013671875, 183.43350219726562, 523.9669799804688, 197.000732421875]}, {"text": "Total", "bbox": [74.43299865722656, 199.37449645996094, 99.4109878540039, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "10", "bbox": [129.4810028076172, 199.37449645996094, 140.87600708007812, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "0", "bbox": [168.77899169921875, 199.37449645996094, 174.4753875732422, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "10", "bbox": [202.3800048828125, 199.37449645996094, 213.77500915527344, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "1", "bbox": [241.67799377441406, 199.37449645996094, 247.3743896484375, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "3", "bbox": [278.12799072265625, 199.37449645996094, 283.8243713378906, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "1", "bbox": [314.5769958496094, 199.37449645996094, 320.27337646484375, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [351.0270080566406, 199.37449645996094, 356.723388671875, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [387.47601318359375, 199.37449645996094, 393.1723937988281, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "1", "bbox": [423.9259948730469, 199.37449645996094, 429.62237548828125, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "1", "bbox": [460.3760070800781, 199.37449645996094, 466.0723876953125, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "33", "bbox": [505.7820129394531, 199.37449645996094, 517.177001953125, 212.9417266845703]}, {"text": "In this problem, you will synthesise and analyse complex A with molecular formula [M(Py)𝑚X𝑛] where:", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 218.28897094726562, 530.77685546875, 254.46755981445312]}, {"text": "- M𝑘+ is an unknown metal cation;", "bbox": [98.70800018310547, 251.84722900390625, 258.8560485839844, 282.97857666015625]}, {"text": "- Py (pyridine);", "bbox": [98.70800018310547, 281.3525085449219, 165.11935424804688, 294.91973876953125]}, {"text": "- X−is either OCN−or SCN−;", "bbox": [98.70800018310547, 276.96221923828125, 232.0016326904297, 308.09356689453125]}, {"text": "- m = 0, 1, 2, 3, ...;", "bbox": [98.70799255371094, 305.26251220703125, 178.5919647216797, 318.8297424316406]}, {"text": "- n = 1, 2, 3, ...", "bbox": [98.70799255371094, 317.2174987792969, 162.02508544921875, 330.78472900390625]}, {"text": "Part A. Synthesis", "bbox": [56.29199981689453, 359.1905822753906, 148.0406951904297, 374.1145935058594]}, {"text": "To synthesise complex A, solutions R1-syn and R2 are used:", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 378.1885070800781, 335.4866943359375, 391.7557373046875]}, {"text": "• Solution R1-syn contains 10.0 mL of an aqueous solution of a M𝑘+ salt with unknown concentration.", "bbox": [72.87200164794922, 381.18621826171875, 538.5777587890625, 417.2051086425781]}, {"text": "• Solution R2 contains 10.0 mL of an aqueous solution of potassium salt of X−with a concentration", "bbox": [72.87200164794922, 399.1192321777344, 538.5888671875, 435.13812255859375]}, {"text": "of 1.03 M.", "bbox": [81.60003662109375, 412.5029602050781, 126.58876037597656, 447.0931091308594]}, {"text": "1. Put the stirrer bar in the 100 mL beaker.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 445.35150146484375, 270.1329040527344, 458.9187316894531]}, {"text": "2. Transfer the whole solution R1-syn to the same beaker.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 463.2845153808594, 343.3974609375, 476.85174560546875]}, {"text": "3. Rinse the vial R1-syn with 1 mL of water using a Pasteur pipette and transfer the remains to the", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 481.2174987792969, 538.5787353515625, 494.78472900390625]}, {"text": "beaker.", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 493.1724853515625, 116.56939697265625, 506.7397155761719]}, {"text": "4. Add dropwise the whole solution R2 using a Pasteur pipette while stirring on the magnetic stirrer.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 511.1044921875, 538.5877685546875, 524.6716918945312]}, {"text": "5. Rinse the vial R2 with 1 mL of water using a Pasteur pipette and transfer the remains to the beaker.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 531.3825073242188, 538.5840454101562, 544.94970703125]}, {"text": "6. Add dropwise the whole pyridine solution (Py) using a Pasteur pipette while stirring.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 549.3145141601562, 477.2081604003906, 562.8826904296875]}, {"text": "7. Continue stirring for 5 minutes.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 569.5924682617188, 231.50611877441406, 583.15966796875]}, {"text": "8. Connect sintered funnel to a round bottom flask to assemble the vacuum filtration apparatus.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 587.5255126953125, 521.625244140625, 601.0927124023438]}, {"text": "9. Filter the product using vacuum filtration and wash it three times with 10 mL portions of water.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 605.45751953125, 528.8634033203125, 619.0247192382812]}, {"text": "10. Once you have finished washing, ask the lab assistant to collect the filtrate to avoid spills. For this,", "bbox": [62.55500030517578, 623.3905029296875, 538.5988159179688, 636.9577026367188]}, {"text": "raise the green card with a question mark, turn off the pump and disconnect the vacuum hose.", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 635.3455200195312, 538.5789794921875, 648.9127197265625]}, {"text": "Remove the filter and hand the flask to the lab assistant. The lab assistant will discard the filtrate", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 647.3004760742188, 538.5941162109375, 660.8677368164062]}, {"text": "and return the empty flask.", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 659.2564697265625, 211.54049682617188, 672.82373046875]}, {"text": "11. Reassemble the filtration setup and let your product dry for 1 hour with the vacuum turned on.", "bbox": [62.55500030517578, 677.1884765625, 538.5657958984375, 690.7556762695312]}, {"text": "During the drying, it is important to use your spatula to break up any aggregates of the product", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 689.1434936523438, 538.5719604492188, 702.710693359375]}, {"text": "formed on the filter.", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 703.4434814453125, 176.11585998535156, 717.0106811523438]}, {"text": "12. After complete drying, carefully transfer your product to the vial labelled “A + Student Code”. For", "bbox": [62.55500030517578, 721.3765258789062, 538.5780639648438, 734.9437255859375]}, {"text": "this you can use the yellow paper provided.", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 733.33154296875, 283.96099853515625, 746.8987426757812]}]}, {"page": 4, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Experiment", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 138.68612670898438, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-4", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Q1.1", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 100.77256774902344, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "The lab assistant will collect your product at the end of the exam. Both you", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 166.2294921875, 480.5718688964844, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "and the lab assistant should sign your answer sheet.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 178.18450927734375, 360.8932800292969, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "The organisers will further dry your product in an oven before measuring the", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 192.4844970703125, 480.5572509765625, 206.05172729492188]}, {"text": "mass, however it is important you have vacuum dried the product for 1 hour", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 204.4394989013672, 480.5476989746094, 218.00672912597656]}, {"text": "and broken up any aggregates to remove the vast majority of the water before", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 216.39450073242188, 480.58892822265625, 229.96173095703125]}, {"text": "putting it in the vial.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 228.35049438476562, 208.10101318359375, 241.917724609375]}, {"text": "(If the product is not transferred to the vial, it will not be collected and ZERO", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 240.3054962158203, 480.5809020996094, 253.8727264404297]}, {"text": "points will be awarded for the synthesis.)", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 252.260498046875, 307.8373107910156, 265.8277282714844]}, {"text": "10 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 166.1544952392578, 519.1494140625, 179.7217254638672]}, {"text": "Part B. Quantitative Analysis", "bbox": [56.29199981689453, 289.3905944824219, 213.55300903320312, 304.3146057128906]}, {"text": "You will use a complexometric titration to determine the concentration of M𝑘+ in solution R1-an. The", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 293.6922302246094, 538.577880859375, 324.8235778808594]}, {"text": "volumetric flask R1-an contains 10.0 mL of M𝑘+ solution with the same concentration as in R1-syn in Part", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 307.0572204589844, 538.58251953125, 343.07611083984375]}, {"text": "A.", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 335.3564758300781, 66.23760223388672, 348.9237060546875]}, {"text": "1. Dilute the R1-an solution in the volumetric flask with H2O up to the mark and mix thoroughly.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 353.28948974609375, 523.5235595703125, 369.05584716796875]}, {"text": "2. Fill the burette with 0.0770 M EDTA.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 356.3069763183594, 248.39964294433594, 390.8971252441406]}, {"text": "3. Add a 10.0 mL aliquot of the diluted solution R1-an using a graduated pipette, 5 mL of ammonia", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 374.2399597167969, 538.5648193359375, 408.8301086425781]}, {"text": "buffer solution (NH3 buffer), and a tip of the plastic spatula of indicator (Eriochrome; the spatula", "bbox": [81.59999084472656, 401.1104736328125, 538.5762939453125, 417.5837097167969]}, {"text": "is inside the sample container) to an Erlenmeyer flask. Close the bottle of NH3 buffer after using", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 413.0654602050781, 538.5708618164062, 429.5387268066406]}, {"text": "it.", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 425.0204772949219, 90.43749237060547, 438.58770751953125]}, {"text": "4. Titrate the mixture with 0.0770 M EDTA solution until the colour turns a stable blue.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 428.0379638671875, 473.2221984863281, 462.62811279296875]}, {"text": "5. Repeat steps 3-4 if necessary.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 460.8865051269531, 221.4198760986328, 474.4537353515625]}, {"text": "Q1.2", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 483.85150146484375, 100.7725601196289, 497.4187316894531]}, {"text": "Record the observed volumes (V0, mL – initial burette reading; V𝑓, mL– final", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 473.98321533203125, 480.57305908203125, 505.11456298828125]}, {"text": "burette reading; T, mL - titre). This table is for your convenience and will not be", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 495.8064880371094, 480.5770568847656, 509.37371826171875]}, {"text": "graded.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 507.761474609375, 150.9754180908203, 521.3286743164062]}, {"text": "0 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 483.7754821777344, 513.4508056640625, 497.34271240234375]}, {"text": "Q1.3", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 542.4855346679688, 100.77256774902344, 556.052734375]}, {"text": "Record your accepted final titre of EDTA (VEDTA, mL).", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 542.4855346679688, 362.8371276855469, 558.2518920898438]}, {"text": "10 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 542.4094848632812, 519.1494750976562, 555.9766845703125]}, {"text": "Q1.4", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 580.552490234375, 100.77256774902344, 594.1196899414062]}, {"text": "Calculate the ratio of X−", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 564.2071533203125, 236.16793823242188, 595.3385009765625]}, {"text": "and M𝑘+ (𝑛𝑋−/𝑛𝑀𝑘+) used in the synthesis according", "bbox": [233.5899658203125, 564.2071533203125, 480.59039306640625, 603.1295166015625]}, {"text": "to your result. Round your answer to two decimal places.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 592.5075073242188, 382.63861083984375, 606.07470703125]}, {"text": "1 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 580.4205322265625, 513.4508056640625, 593.9877319335938]}, {"text": "Part C. Qualitative Analysis", "bbox": [56.29199981689453, 632.9246215820312, 204.77491760253906, 647.8486328125]}, {"text": "In this part, you need to perform different chemical tests to identify the components of complex A.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 651.9224853515625, 517.630615234375, 665.4896850585938]}, {"text": "1. Prepare a 0.4 mL solution of complex A in the Eppendorf tube by adding the solvent with a Pasteur", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 654.9400024414062, 538.5587768554688, 689.5301513671875]}, {"text": "pipette from the Eppendorf tube labelled Solvent until the 0.4 mL mark. If the sample has not", "bbox": [81.5989990234375, 669.239013671875, 538.5733032226562, 703.8291625976562]}, {"text": "dissolved completely, shake the tube and use the supernatant for the tests below.", "bbox": [81.5989990234375, 696.1095581054688, 463.4361877441406, 709.6767578125]}, {"text": "2. Prepare a 0.4 mL solution of the indicator Dithizone (Dithiz.) in the Eppendorf tube by adding the", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 699.126953125, 538.5530395507812, 733.7171020507812]}, {"text": "solvent with a Pasteur pipette from the Eppendorf tube labelled Solvent until the 0.4 mL mark. The", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 713.4269409179688, 538.5711669921875, 748.01708984375]}, {"text": "structure of the indicator is given below.", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 740.2974853515625, 269.7344055175781, 753.8646850585938]}]}, {"page": 5, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Experiment", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 138.68612670898438, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-5", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "3. Take four empty Eppendorf tubes and transfer 1 drop of the solution of A obtained to each.", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 245.978515625, 513.0889282226562, 259.5457458496094]}, {"text": "4. Perform the individual tests T1−T4 by adding the following reagents to each of the four Eppendorf", "bbox": [68.2509994506836, 263.9105224609375, 538.5606079101562, 277.4777526855469]}, {"text": "tubes:", "bbox": [81.60000610351562, 278.1575012207031, 110.54202270507812, 291.7247314453125]}, {"text": "• T1: 2 drops of Fe3+(acidified Fe(NO3)3)", "bbox": [72.87200164794922, 279.7452087402344, 264.9295349121094, 315.7641296386719]}, {"text": "• T2: 2 drops of the prepared Dithizone solution", "bbox": [72.87200164794922, 314.02252197265625, 301.2354431152344, 327.5897521972656]}, {"text": "• T3: 2 drops of Cu2+(CuSO4)", "bbox": [72.87200164794922, 317.5232238769531, 211.80255126953125, 353.5431213378906]}, {"text": "• T4: 2 drops of Cu2+(CuSO4) followed by 3 drops of CH2Cl2 and shake", "bbox": [72.87200164794922, 337.4662170410156, 407.923583984375, 373.4861145019531]}, {"text": "You may perform additional tests; for this you are provided with extra equipment and chemicals (e.g.,", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 371.7434997558594, 538.5645751953125, 385.31072998046875]}, {"text": "solutions of Py and X−). Additional information: 𝜌(CH2Cl2) = 1.32 g/cm3", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 369.2672424316406, 382.1337890625, 405.2861328125]}, {"text": "Q1.5", "bbox": [78.6080322265625, 408.5235290527344, 100.77259826660156, 422.09075927734375]}, {"text": "Tick the correct box(es) corresponding to your observation(s) in T1 - T3.", "bbox": [114.69256591796875, 408.52349853515625, 448.8486328125, 422.09075927734375]}, {"text": "(a) No visible change", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 420.4784851074219, 212.53900146484375, 434.04571533203125]}, {"text": "(b) Formation of precipitate", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 432.4334716796875, 243.7499237060547, 446.0007019042969]}, {"text": "(c) Solution became colourless", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 444.3884582519531, 257.36273193359375, 457.9556884765625]}, {"text": "(d) Solution became red or pink", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 456.3444519042969, 262.3920593261719, 469.91168212890625]}, {"text": "3 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 408.44244384765625, 513.4508666992188, 422.0096740722656]}, {"text": "Q1.6", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 491.0144958496094, 100.77256774902344, 504.58172607421875]}, {"text": "Tick the correct box(es) corresponding to your observation(s) in T4.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 491.0144958496094, 429.0006408691406, 504.58172607421875]}, {"text": "(a) The aqueous phase changed colour", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 502.969482421875, 296.6644287109375, 516.5366821289062]}, {"text": "(b) The aqueous phase did not change colour", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 514.9244995117188, 326.60009765625, 528.49169921875]}, {"text": "(c) The CH2Cl2 phase changed colour", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 526.8794555664062, 289.1106872558594, 542.9376220703125]}, {"text": "(d) The CH2Cl2 phase did not change colour", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 538.8344116210938, 319.95233154296875, 554.8926391601562]}, {"text": "1 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 490.8824462890625, 513.4508666992188, 504.4496765136719]}, {"text": "Q1.7", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 573.655517578125, 100.77256774902344, 587.2227172851562]}, {"text": "The above tests T1−T4 are designed to identify the components of the complex", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 573.655517578125, 480.5789489746094, 587.2227172851562]}, {"text": "A. Tick the box(es) that correctly describe(s) the result(s) of each test.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 585.6104736328125, 437.4569396972656, 599.177734375]}, {"text": "(a) Identifies presence of metal M𝑘+", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 583.6221923828125, 283.1347961425781, 614.7535400390625]}, {"text": "(b) Identifies presence of ligand X−", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 595.5772705078125, 277.8179931640625, 626.7085571289062]}, {"text": "(c) Identifies presence of ligand Py", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 623.8775024414062, 275.7513122558594, 637.4447021484375]}, {"text": "(d) Identifies absence of ligand Py", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 635.83251953125, 272.8885192871094, 649.3997192382812]}, {"text": "4 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 573.5435180664062, 513.4508666992188, 587.1107177734375]}, {"text": "Q1.8", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 672.9085083007812, 100.77256774902344, 686.4757080078125]}, {"text": "Identify ligand X−and metal M𝑘+ with its charge in complex A.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 656.563232421875, 410.70458984375, 687.6945190429688]}, {"text": "2 pt", "bbox": [495.449951171875, 672.8274536132812, 513.4508056640625, 686.3946533203125]}]}, {"page": 6, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Experiment", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 138.68612670898438, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q1-6", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "Q1.9", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 168.58151245117188, 100.77256774902344, 182.14874267578125]}, {"text": "From the list below, choose the correct description of M𝑘+/X−stoichiometry in", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 152.23721313476562, 480.5881652832031, 188.25613403320312]}, {"text": "the synthesis based on your reported results. Consider as little as an additional", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 180.53750610351562, 480.5755920410156, 194.104736328125]}, {"text": "1 mol% as an excess of the reagent.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 192.4925079345703, 281.6748352050781, 206.0597381591797]}, {"text": "(a) M𝑘+ and X−were used in a stoichiometric amount", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 189.51222229003906, 365.0624084472656, 220.64356994628906]}, {"text": "(b) M𝑘+ was used in excess", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 201.46722412109375, 241.46170043945312, 232.59857177734375]}, {"text": "(c) X−was used in excess", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 213.42221069335938, 232.2187042236328, 244.55355834960938]}, {"text": "1 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 168.4504852294922, 513.4508056640625, 182.01771545410156]}, {"text": "Q1.10", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 263.67352294921875, 106.47117614746094, 277.2407531738281]}, {"text": "Write the molecular formula of complex A assuming it follows the 18-electron", "bbox": [114.69254302978516, 263.67352294921875, 480.6005554199219, 277.2407531738281]}, {"text": "rule.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 275.6285095214844, 135.8223419189453, 289.19573974609375]}, {"text": "1 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 263.54150390625, 513.4508666992188, 277.1087341308594]}]}]